ng:Self_Portrait_with_Monkey_creator_Frida_Kahlo a sem:Event ;
    ng:object "Frida Kahlo" ;
    ng:property "creator" ;
    ng:subject "Self-Portrait with Monkey" ;
    sem:hasTimeStamp "1938-01-01"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:comment "Self-Portrait with Monkey (Autorretrato con mono in Spanish) is an oil on masonite painting by Mexican artist Frida Kahlo, commissioned in 1938 by A. Conger Goodyear, then president of the Museum of Modern Art in New York City. It is one of the many self-portraits painted by Kahlo for friends and patrons during her career. The commission came after Goodyear attended Kahlo's first solo exhibition in November 1938 at the Julien Levy Gallery in New York." .

ng:Self_Portrait_with_Monkey_depicts_Frida_Kahlo a sem:Event ;
    ng:object "Frida Kahlo" ;
    ng:property "depicts" ;
    ng:subject "Self-Portrait with Monkey" ;
    sem:hasTimeStamp "1938-01-01"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:comment "Self-Portrait with Monkey (Autorretrato con mono in Spanish) is an oil on masonite painting by Mexican artist Frida Kahlo, commissioned in 1938 by A. Conger Goodyear, then president of the Museum of Modern Art in New York City. It is one of the many self-portraits painted by Kahlo for friends and patrons during her career. The commission came after Goodyear attended Kahlo's first solo exhibition in November 1938 at the Julien Levy Gallery in New York." .

ng:Self_Portrait_with_Monkey_owned_by_Frida_Kahlo a sem:Event ;
    ng:object "Frida Kahlo" ;
    ng:property "owned by" ;
    ng:subject "Self-Portrait with Monkey" ;
    sem:hasTimeStamp "1939-01-03"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:comment "Self-Portrait with Monkey (Autorretrato con mono in Spanish) is an oil on masonite painting by Mexican artist Frida Kahlo, commissioned in 1938 by A. Conger Goodyear, then president of the Museum of Modern Art in New York City. It is one of the many self-portraits painted by Kahlo for friends and patrons during her career. The commission came after Goodyear attended Kahlo's first solo exhibition in November 1938 at the Julien Levy Gallery in New York." .

ng:Self_Portrait_with_Thorn_Necklace_and_Hummingbird_creator_Frida_Kahlo a sem:Event ;
    ng:object "Frida Kahlo" ;
    ng:property "creator" ;
    ng:subject "Self-Portrait with Thorn Necklace and Hummingbird" ;
    sem:hasTimeStamp "1940-01-01"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:comment "Self-Portrait with Thorn Necklace and Hummingbird (Spanish: Autorretrato con Collar de Espinas y Colibrí) is a 1940 self-portrait by Mexican painter Frida Kahlo which also includes a black cat, a monkey, and two dragonflies. It was painted after Kahlo's divorce from Diego Rivera and the end of her affair with photographer Nickolas Muray. Muray bought the portrait shortly after it was painted, and it is currently part of the Nickolas Muray collection at the Harry Ransom Center at the University of Texas at Austin." .

ng:Self_Portrait_with_Thorn_Necklace_and_Hummingbird_depicts_Frida_Kahlo a sem:Event ;
    ng:object "Frida Kahlo" ;
    ng:property "depicts" ;
    ng:subject "Self-Portrait with Thorn Necklace and Hummingbird" ;
    sem:hasTimeStamp "1940-01-01"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:comment "Self-Portrait with Thorn Necklace and Hummingbird (Spanish: Autorretrato con Collar de Espinas y Colibrí) is a 1940 self-portrait by Mexican painter Frida Kahlo which also includes a black cat, a monkey, and two dragonflies. It was painted after Kahlo's divorce from Diego Rivera and the end of her affair with photographer Nickolas Muray. Muray bought the portrait shortly after it was painted, and it is currently part of the Nickolas Muray collection at the Harry Ransom Center at the University of Texas at Austin." .

ng:Still_Life_Pitahayas_creator_Frida_Kahlo a sem:Event ;
    ng:object "Frida Kahlo" ;
